# The bracket of the walk to 10^200, by checkpoints

The bracket ends `log2Lo 3 2663 1330` and `log2Hi 3 2663 1330` come from 1330 squarings
(`powBounds`). Computed in one go, the kernel unfolds them lazily and needs 2912 s and 18.6 GB.
Here they are cut at the states after 100, 200, ..., 1300 and 1330 squarings, written as
literals (computed by a compiled run; the kernel checks each chunk from the one before,
`farPow200_100_step` to `farPow200_1330_step`). Joined by `powBounds_of_chunk`, they give
the bracket ends as literals (`farLo200_eq`, `farHi200_eq`), so the stretches of the walk
(`PowDiffFarRhin1` to `PowDiffFarLow4`) start from numbers instead of the squarings.
Each number is written in blocks of 80 digits. A heavy check (see the README).
-/

namespace PowDiff

open AcceleratedCollatz

/-- A chunk of n squarings from the state after m squarings gives the state after m + n. -/
theorem powBounds_of_chunk {u B m n k : ℕ} {t t' : PowBounds} (h : powBounds u B m = t)
    (hs : (powSq B)^[n] t = t') (hk : m + n = k) : powBounds u B k = t' := by
  subst hk
  rw [← hs, ← h, powBounds, powBounds, Nat.add_comm, Function.iterate_add_apply]

